  "definition": "A spacecraft eclipse power budget demonstrates that stored energy can support required loads throughout darkness and that the following sunlit interval can restore the battery. It is an energy balance in watt-hours (Wh), coupled to instantaneous power limits in watts (W). Ampere-hours (Ah) measure charge; converting Ah to Wh requires the battery voltage over the discharge, rather than an arbitrary nominal voltage.",
